\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8.6}{\ignorespaces Mean per-entry time (ms, completed entries only) and timeout share, one real routine pass per category at each category's own default sweep. \texttt  {std\_rec}/\texttt  {std\_loop} abbreviate \texttt  {deriv\_std\_rec}/\texttt  {deriv\_std\_loop}; \texttt  {to\%} is the percentage of that category's entries that timed out (0 crashes in A--H). $^\dagger $H's row is from the run that surfaced the \texttt  {P29}/\texttt  {P31} labeling bug of Section~\ref {sec:eval-agreement} (32 entries, one row's non-match side not yet removed); the fix drops one input but does not change how long any of the remaining ones take to parse, so the timing figures stand, just against a since-corrected entry count (28 after the fix).}}{77}{table.caption.48}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:patho-timing-smoke}{{8.6}{77}{Mean per-entry time (ms, completed entries only) and timeout share, one real routine pass per category at each category's own default sweep. \texttt {std\_rec}/\texttt {std\_loop} abbreviate \texttt {deriv\_std\_rec}/\texttt {deriv\_std\_loop}; \texttt {to\%} is the percentage of that category's entries that timed out (0 crashes in A--H). $^\dagger $H's row is from the run that surfaced the \texttt {P29}/\texttt {P31} labeling bug of Section~\ref {sec:eval-agreement} (32 entries, one row's non-match side not yet removed); the fix drops one input but does not change how long any of the remaining ones take to parse, so the timing figures stand, just against a since-corrected entry count (28 after the fix)}{table.caption.48}{}}
